# Database migrations

Start PostgreSQL from the repository root with `docker compose up -d db`.
Compose publishes PostgreSQL on host port `5433`; set `DATABASE_URL` in
`backend/.env` to match `backend/.env.example`.

Apply all migrations from the `backend` directory:

```bash
python -m alembic upgrade head
```

On Windows, call the virtual environment's Python:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
```

## Revisions

| Revision | What it does |
|---|---|
| `0001_initial_schema` | Users, teams, memberships, work items, comments, events, idempotency keys and outbox tables. |
| `0002_hardening` | Adds `work_items.next_action` and makes `item_events` append-only with a database trigger. |
| `0003_notifications` | Adds the notifications table with a unique (event, user) key. |

Create a new migration after changing `app/models.py`:

```bash
python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
```

Review the generated file before applying it.